<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para><span>Is there anything unique about the method used to solve \(–\frac12x\leq1\)? Explain.</span></para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <span>Yes. The inequality contains a less than or equal to symbol \((\leq)\). However, in the solution there is a greater than or equal to symbol \((\geq)\). When using the Multiplication and Division Properties of Inequality, you must reverse the symbol when you multiply or divide by a negative number.</span>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
